.TH "PERCH-MAIL-FETCH" "1" "" "perch" "perch manual"
.SH NAME
perch\-mail\-fetch \- fetch raw messages
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B perch mail fetch [OPTIONS]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Fetch complete RFC 5322 messages selected by UID, query, or \-\-all. The default format writes one .eml per message when \-\-dest is a directory, or raw bytes to stdout for a single message.
.PP
mbox writes a standard mbox stream. maildir creates tmp/new/cur and preserves message flags.
.PP
Aliases: get.
.SH NOTES
.IP \(bu 2
BODY.PEEK[] is used unless \-\-mark\-seen is set.
.IP \(bu 2
Writing eml to stdout requires exactly one message.
.IP \(bu 2
\-\-dest is a directory for eml/maildir and a file for mbox.
.IP \(bu 2
Existing files are not overwritten unless \-\-overwrite is passed.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-username, \-u <value>
account username (env PERCH_IMAP_USER)
.TP
.B \-\-password <value>
account password (prefer PERCH_IMAP_PASSWORD or \-\-password\-file)
.TP
.B \-\-password\-file <value>
read the account password from a file
.TP
.B \-\-password\-stdin
read the account password from stdin
.TP
.B \-\-timeout <value>
connection timeout (default: 30s)
.TP
.B \-\-config <value>
configuration file (default: ~/.config/perch/perch.yaml)
.TP
.B \-\-mailbox, \-m <value>
mailbox to fetch from (default: "INBOX")
.TP
.B \-\-query, \-q <value>
search expression
.TP
.B \-\-uids <value>
explicit UID set, for example 1,3:5,10:*
.TP
.B \-\-all
fetch every message in the mailbox
.TP
.B \-\-limit, \-n <value>
maximum messages (0 means unlimited) (default: 0)
.TP
.B \-\-format, \-f <value>
eml, mbox, or maildir (default: "eml")
.TP
.B \-\-dest, \-d, \-o <value>
destination directory (eml/maildir) or file (mbox); default stdout
.TP
.B \-\-mark\-seen
let the server set \\Seen (default uses BODY.PEEK)
.TP
.B \-\-overwrite
overwrite an existing eml/mbox destination
.TP
.B \-\-reverse
fetch newest first instead of oldest first
.TP
.B \-\-server, \-s <value>
IMAP server (imaps://host, imap://host, or host[:port]); defaults from \-\-config
.TP
.B \-\-plaintext
connect to IMAP without TLS (use only on trusted networks)
.TP
.B \-\-starttls
require STARTTLS for IMAP
.TP
.B \-\-insecure
skip IMAP TLS certificate verification
.TP
.B \-\-ca\-file <value>
PEM CA bundle used to verify the IMAP server certificate
.TP
.B \-\-help, \-h
show help
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
perch mail fetch \-\-uids 42 > message.eml

perch mail fetch \-q 'from:alice' \-\-format mbox > alice.mbox

perch mail fetch \-q 'unseen' \-\-format maildir \-\-dest ~/Mail

perch mail fetch \-q 'unseen' \-\-dest ./messages
.fi
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B PERCH_IMAP_USER
default account username
.TP
.B PERCH_IMAP_PASSWORD
account password
.SH SEE ALSO
.PP
\fBperch\fR(1), \fBperch\-mail\fR(1)
